                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "2804fc7e-4210-34cb-b7f3-cb40df8fa510",
                        "entry_id": "60c23c2e-4277-3991-903c-9e8018f146db",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Polychore dont les cellules sont 8 cubes."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "57f029c8-8a09-4f82-9162-fc97f07abb36",
                        "source_entry_id": "60c23c2e-4277-3991-903c-9e8018f146db",
                        "source_sense_id": "2804fc7e-4210-34cb-b7f3-cb40df8fa510",
                        "target_lang_word": "tesseract",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "tesseract",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c3dd6e8d-df37-3c2f-a18f-538c0c396471",
                                        "entry_id": "e47ec1fa-aa70-3f86-b943-c34661bcd969",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The four-dimensional analogue of a cube; a 4D polytope bounded by eight cubes (analogously to the way a cube is bounded by six squares)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b185aba3-a0a5-437e-87e8-a050fb49c695",
                                                "sense_id": "c3dd6e8d-df37-3c2f-a18f-538c0c396471",
                                                "text": "[…]then it would trace out a higher cube, or tesseract, and each of the six surrounding cubes, carried on in the same motion, would trace tesseracts also,[…]."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9437c284-1a9d-4ca0-8ad9-79741f844241",
                                                "sense_id": "c3dd6e8d-df37-3c2f-a18f-538c0c396471",
                                                "text": "Hence the cube determined by these axes is the face of the tesseract which we now have before us."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e518cfa9-1841-304c-800f-28bce73c41f3",
                                        "entry_id": "e47ec1fa-aa70-3f86-b943-c34661bcd969",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any of various fictional mechanisms that explain extradimensional, superluminal, or time travel outside the geometry of the physical universe."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2d52cb9c-8483-4ca9-a276-decc123bb932",
                                                "sense_id": "e518cfa9-1841-304c-800f-28bce73c41f3",
                                                "text": "\"I shall just sit down for a moment and pop on my boots and then I'll be on my way. Speaking of ways, pet, by the way, there is such a thing as a tesseract.\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3a65aa64-5406-47c7-b01b-886e7e18cf55",
                                                "sense_id": "e518cfa9-1841-304c-800f-28bce73c41f3",
                                                "text": "When the Tesseract's energy levels spiked, Selvig proved unable to stop it and Loki arrived on Earth via a Tesseract-created portal."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5d3f447a-73d3-415f-aacc-8ff57e4a2eae",
                                                "sense_id": "e518cfa9-1841-304c-800f-28bce73c41f3",
                                                "text": "Cooper sees his younger self due to the tesseract in Interstellar."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ef1ff875-a1b3-49e0-bacc-26c45f84654b",
                        "source_entry_id": "60c23c2e-4277-3991-903c-9e8018f146db",
                        "source_sense_id": "2804fc7e-4210-34cb-b7f3-cb40df8fa510",
                        "target_lang_word": "8-cell",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "8-cell",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1c2576fa-6e28-3fd2-a9bd-543a7145a849",
                                        "entry_id": "98badb19-39b4-35c3-9555-9894b4507e11",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A four-dimensional polytope, analogous to a cube, whose eight bounding facets are cubes; a tesseract."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5bfe37ee-1441-4e4d-98f2-b73849e00b3e",
                                                "sense_id": "1c2576fa-6e28-3fd2-a9bd-543a7145a849",
                                                "text": "According to this table the tetrahedron corresponds to the 5-cell, the cube to the 8-cell (\"hypercube\"), the octahedron to the 16-cell, the dodecahedron to the 120-cell and the icosahedron to the 600-cell. The 24-cell is an additional body in four-dimensional space which is dual to itself."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "51fe86c5-10b1-4315-a7bf-738357e6d4b5",
                                                "sense_id": "1c2576fa-6e28-3fd2-a9bd-543a7145a849",
                                                "text": "Similarly in dimension eight there is the quaternionic projective plane which we can think of as a 4-sphere with an 8-cell attached, and in dimension sixteen there is a Cayley projective plane which has similar properties."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a8a1e0cf-8039-4c95-b532-053332d3c4a3",
                                                "sense_id": "1c2576fa-6e28-3fd2-a9bd-543a7145a849",
                                                "text": "Of these nine, five are finite structures in Euclidean space and include the simplex, {3,3,3} (or 5-cell), the four-dimensional cube {4,3,3} (or 8-cell) and its dual {3,3,4} (or 16-cell), and the 120-cell {5,3,3} and its dual {3,3,5} (or 600-cell)."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ef65302c-18bd-43a5-a556-11f8ed5befb3",
                        "source_entry_id": "60c23c2e-4277-3991-903c-9e8018f146db",
                        "source_sense_id": "2804fc7e-4210-34cb-b7f3-cb40df8fa510",
                        "target_lang_word": "octachoron",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "octachoron",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4916cf49-c626-34e1-8b7e-cd75d4c22ae2",
                                        "entry_id": "b98680be-c5d1-391b-a3a0-61890dc4ec02",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A four-dimensional object analogous to a cube, constructed out of eight cubes."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cddfecc1-682f-428a-b749-613fcdfeac02",
                                                "sense_id": "4916cf49-c626-34e1-8b7e-cd75d4c22ae2",
                                                "text": "Our 16-point 4D constellation is described by the set {(±1,±1,±1,±1)}, which is indeed the set of vertices of a tesseract (i.e., a regular octachoron) [4]."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cd654a3e-cacb-4512-aac6-f788ce57025c",
                                                "sense_id": "4916cf49-c626-34e1-8b7e-cd75d4c22ae2",
                                                "text": "The Schlegel diagram from this figure is a projection of a regular octachoron from the 4-D space to the 3-D space through a point beyond one of its facets."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "885d434d-55b6-4ecd-acbb-2f4117d7a19b",
                                                "sense_id": "4916cf49-c626-34e1-8b7e-cd75d4c22ae2",
                                                "text": "...completing the notation for the vertices of an elementary lattice octachoron."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "c2ba5ec4-42dd-4d49-b4f0-470b05e936a9",
                        "source_entry_id": "60c23c2e-4277-3991-903c-9e8018f146db",
